>How can chaotic Orcus summon lawful Baalzebub?

Orcus can cast summon nasties (as you know).

When summon nasties is cast in Hell, there is a 1 in 10 chance that it
will summon a single monster using the function msummon() (minion.c),
rather than a pack of monsters selected from the "nasties" list.

msummon() takes a single argument, which is a pointer to a monster.  If
this pointer is NULL, the function proceeds as if it pointed to an
instance of the Wizard of Yendor.  The Wizard of Yendor is unaligned,
and hence if the summon nasties spell takes this path, demon princes and
lords of any alignment may be summoned.
